ity looks solid: a Piotroski score of 7/9 and cash conversion of 1.08x.","Operating margin is running 16pp above its own historical average, a peak-margin risk if conditions normalise.","It spends 1.9% of revenue on R&D and 0.5% on stock compensation."],"hlth":["Leverage is moderate at 2.4x net debt to EBITDA ($4.9B of cash against $45.3B of debt), above the 1.5x gate, with interest covered 9.4x.","No distress or manipulation flags (Altman Z 4.2, in the safe zone).","The current ratio of 0.96 means short-term liabilities exceed current assets.","Working capital ties up about 234 days of sales, a drag on cash generation."],"growth":["Revenue has compounded at -20.4% over 3 years, -11.8% over 5 years and -5.8% over 10 years, so the decline is deepening, and it has been lumpy (year-to-year swings of 15%).","At current returns, reinvesting 10% of profits supports about 4.4% a year of fundamental growth, enough to sustain growth.","Free cash flow has compounded 3.0% a year over five years, short of the 5% durability bar.","Margins are expanding (+1.3% trend).","Capex runs only 0.8x depreciation (3.9% of sales), so the asset base is being harvested rather than grown.","Its Rule of 40 score is 14, below the 40 that marks a healthy growth business."],"own":["Insiders hold little stock (0.2%), and institutions hold 84%.","It returns 3.0% a year to shareholders (3.5% in dividends).","It has paid a dividend for 17 consecutive years, raising it 3.2% a year over the last five."],"people":["With about 84,900 employees, each generates about $479K of revenue, in line with the Consumer Defensive median, and revenue has fallen 2.6% a year across its filed history.","That works out to $126K of free cash flow per employee.","CEO pay is $7.1M (15x revenue per employee), and compensation governance scores well (1/10, lower is better).","Stock compensation averages $2K per employee."]},"profile":{"v":"AVOID","conv":62,"head":"Avoid: priced 41% above its fair value of $131.","pros":["Compo